title: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Read the document list
route: /payers/summit?tab=documents
intro: The 'Clinical documentation' group of Rules & Instructions. A link with ?tab=documents (the older Documents tab) opens the group and scrolls it into view. It shows what the payer wants to see for each level of care, as a plain numbered list with no status on any row; the same group holds the chart checker and any clinical-criteria rules. The list is closed on a one-line summary and opens on a click. The list is chosen with 'Level of care'. In the demo the lists are per level of care (Residential 3.5, IOP, PHP, Detox); request type only changes the workflow, not this list. New case checks a draft's documents against the saved list for its payer and level of care.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Open 'Clinical documentation' in Rules & Instructions\nor follow a link with ?tab=documents"
screen tab "Clinical documentation group (opened and in view)\nBanner above the groups if edits wait\nThen 'Level of care' and 'Edit list', the closed list,\n'Try it on a case', and clinical-criteria rules"
screen card "Closed section 'What Summit wants for Residential 3.5'\n'Nine documents: ASAM multidimensional assessment,\nPsychiatric evaluation or H&P, and 7 more.'"
click op "Click the section (or Enter, Space)\nIt opens and closes, and stays open when 'Level of care' changes"
process dflt "Opens on Residential 3.5 every time\nthe view or the payer changes\nThe list is closed again"
input lc "Pick 'Level of care'\nResidential 3.5, IOP, PHP, Detox"
process sw "Title, count and list switch to that level\nFor Summit: Residential 9, IOP 6, PHP 7, Detox 8"
screen ol "Open: numbered list\nNumber, document name in bold,\nwhat it must show in grey\nThen 'The agents ask for each one before they write a word.'"
process ex "Example row\nASAM multidimensional assessment\nEvery dimension, dated within 7 days"
decision any "Is the list empty?"
toast em "'This list is empty. Add the documents Summit asks for.'"
process pdiff "Payers differ a little\nLakeshore adds 'Fax cover sheet' to every list\nHarborview adds a Part D medication list and a Medicare eligibility check\nEvergreen adds a call log with the reviewer"
process one "One document reads 'One document.'\nNumbers up to fifteen are spelled out"
decision dU "Edits saved but not yet applied?"
toast bU "'1 edit applies to new drafts only'\nNew drafts use this at once. Sent requests keep\nwhat they were sent with."
click ce "Click 'Edit list'"
goto gE "Continues in: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Edit the document list"
goto gC "Continues in: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Try it on a case"
goto gU "Continues in: Payers › Edits waiting › Update drafts"
process aft "A payer change can add rows\nCardinal's 2026.3 change adds 'Remaining treatment goals'\n(Named in the latest progress note) to Residential 3.5,\nIOP and PHP when the change is updated.\nEvergreen's change adds 'Notice call reference number'"
goto gA "Continues in: Payers › History & Changes › Review and apply a change"

s1 --> tab --> dU
dU -->|Yes| bU --> gU
dU -->|No| card
bU --> card
card --> dflt --> lc --> sw
card --> op --> ol
sw -.-> op
ol --> ex --> any
any -->|Yes| em
any -->|No| pdiff
em -.-> ce
pdiff -.-> one
pdiff --> aft --> gA
tab --> ce --> gE
tab --> gC
